From 71f7739a1599733961b8e7f02d0fa5c24e4bd70e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:19:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/65] ui: report the screen's pixel ratio before the main
 window exists

skin_window_create() samples the device pixel ratio before the first
showWindow(), when the top-level container has no QWindow yet, and
slot_getDevicePixelRatio() answered 1.0 then. The first native GL subwindow
was therefore created at the logical display size in device pixels: on a
150% monitor it covered only the top-left 2/3 of a 1272x720 window. With the
Vulkan swapchain nothing is presented into it before the guest's first
frame, so that part kept the grey skin background (0x808080) painted just
before it appeared while the rest of the window was repainted black. The
kEventScreenChanged queued by the constructor later re-reads the ratio and
recreates the subwindow at full size, which is why guest frames fill the
window.

Without a QWindow, fall back to QWidget::screen() (the screen the container
is about to appear on, else the primary screen) so the first subwindow gets
the right size.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: Iad6e5885b0ad0c5b9595a143600f78a0fad04c7c
---
 .../src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp        | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp b/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp
index ba88402db..78110f656 100644
--- a/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp
+++ b/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp
@@ -2175,8 +2175,15 @@ void EmulatorQtWindow::slot_fill(SkinSurface* s,
 void EmulatorQtWindow::slot_getDevicePixelRatio(double* out_dpr,
                                                 QSemaphore* semaphore) {
     QSemaphoreReleaser semReleaser(semaphore);
-    auto screen = window()->windowHandle() ? window()->windowHandle()->screen()
-                                           : nullptr;
+    // skin_window_create() asks for the ratio before the first showWindow(),
+    // when the top-level window has no QWindow yet. Answering 1.0 there made
+    // the first native GL subwindow logical-size in device pixels (2/3 of the
+    // display area at 150%), so until the guest's first frame only that
+    // top-left part kept the skin background. Use the screen the window is
+    // about to be shown on instead; QWidget::screen() falls back to the
+    // primary screen.
+    QWindow* handle = window()->windowHandle();
+    QScreen* screen = handle ? handle->screen() : window()->screen();
     *out_dpr = screen ? screen->devicePixelRatio() : 1.0;
 }
 
